  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic Security and Resilience Partnership Facility with Indo-Pacific countries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The action will contribute to the implementation of the European Economic Security Strategy[1] by strengthening partnerships and cooperation with selected Indo-Pacific partner countries on economic security.The action will contribute to the objectives of the Regional Multi-annual Indicative Programme (2021-2027) for Asia and the Pacific, and in particular to the Specific Objective 1 on `Reinforced cooperation with the EU&#xbf;s partners in Asia and the Pacific to strengthen multilateralism (partnerships for multilateralism) by effectively implementing the EU Strategy for Cooperation in the Indo-Pacific (2021)[2], and enhance the EU&#xbf;s role and profile as a global actor in Asia and the Pacific.&#xbf;[1] https://ec.europa.eu/commission/presscorner/detail/en/ip_23_3358[2] https://www.eeas.europa.eu/eu-indo-pacific-strategy-topic_en</narrative>
  </description>
